229
00:17:05,319 --> 00:17:09,860
A board can expect a scout to be neat in appearance and properly uniformed.

230
00:17:09,859 --> 00:17:13,780
Now, I wouldn't expect a scout who didn't own a uniform to show up in one,

231
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:16,459
And I've never made it a requirement to join scouts.

232
00:17:16,579 --> 00:17:20,479
But I mean, shouldn't we expect them to wear a uniform to a board of review?

233
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:22,679
I'm not trying to be argumentative,

234
00:17:22,719 --> 00:17:24,099
I'm just looking for a little clarity.

235
00:17:24,579 --> 00:17:27,939
I've learned that there's a lot in scouting that is kind of a gray area

236
00:17:27,939 --> 00:17:30,760
And I'm learning that there are probably very good reasons for that.

237
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:35,260
I want to feel like I'm doing right by the boys and the organization. in the grand scheme of things,

238
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:39,780
If we encourage uniforms at all, shouldn't we encourage them to be worn at a board of review?

239
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:42,000
And that's from Heidi in Indiana.

240
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:46,419
So first off, Heidi, thanks for getting in touch, sending me an email.

241
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,060
Glad you're listening to the podcast

242
00:17:49,139 --> 00:17:51,159
And I do remember talking about this.

243
00:17:51,159 --> 00:17:55,820
And what I was attempting to illustrate was that we- and that includes me-

244
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:03,139
tend to accept certain traditions and practices in scouting as though they were a matter of formal written policy.

245
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:11,740
At one time in my troop we would turn a boy away from a board of review if he didn't have his uniform on.

246
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,440
Now I questioned that policy,

247
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:17,020
I just got to thinking about it.

248
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:18,020
So I did a little studying

249
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:24,760
And I could not find any official statement that said a scout must be in uniform to qualify for a board of review,

250
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:33,300
And not only that, that scouts were actually never required to own or wear a uniform as a matter of official policy.

251
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:43,540
Now the policy that you quote, Heidi, reads: a board can expect a scout to be neat in appearance and properly uniformed,

252
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:51,060
Which is a much different statement than a board can require a scout to be neat in appearance and properly uniformed.

253
00:18:51,620 --> 00:19:00,540
And you know, I read exactly that statement actually, when I kind of made this discovery for myself

254
00:19:01,139 --> 00:19:06,220
Once I understood that we shouldn't be turning boys away from a board of review if they didn't wear their uniform.

255
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:10,680
I didn't just kind of line up the scouts one evening and say:

256
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:13,399
Hey, by the way, I found out, you never have to wear a uniform,

257
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:14,680
So just do whatever you want.

258
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,200
No, not the way we handled it.

259
00:19:17,659 --> 00:19:20,300
What we did is we talked with our adult leaders and said:

260
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:21,120
Hey, you know what?

261
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:26,280
Here's what real policy is, and why does it say this and how should we react to it?

262
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:30,379
And the reason that the policy is the way that it is

263
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:39,340
is that we don't want to deny scouts participation in any part of scouting based on a uniform or a lack of a uniform.

264
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:41,399
Now we really encourage it.

265
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:45,200
And boys want to have a uniform.

266
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:48,060
Yes, that's exactly what I said.

267
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:50,200
They want to have it and they want to wear it.

268
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:52,200
That's been my experience.

269
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:53,760
They complain about it.

270
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:58,480
They don't when they're younger, they don't like wearing it in front of other people.

271
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:00,900
But they want to have a uniform

272
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:11,560
And I would say we have. you know, 80, 90% of our scouts are in uniform at meetings and boards of review and outings and all that stuff

273
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:15,880
If they're out of uniform. we try not to make a big giant deal out of it.

274
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:20,800
Now, there's a number of reasons why a scout might not have a uniform.

275
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:22,840
I mean, it might be his own fault.

276
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:28,320
He might be, you know, being forgetful or irresponsible or just plain willful.

277
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:32,300
None of these are surprising in a scout age boy.

278
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:40,379
But there's also a number of reasons why a scout wouldn't have a uniform that are beyond his control.

279
00:20:40,879 --> 00:20:42,580
Maybe his parents can't afford a uniform.

280
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:45,800
Maybe his uniform's in the wash and it didn't get clean.

281
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:52,680
Maybe his parents are being forgetful or irresponsible or just plain willful.

282
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:55,520
You know there's all kinds of reasons.

283
00:20:57,020 --> 00:21:04,960
But the broad underlying concept of all this is that we don't ever look for reasons to penalize a scout,

284
00:21:05,660 --> 00:21:09,320
especially reasons that are demonstrably beyond his control.

285
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:15,780
We're always looking for ways to express positive reinforcement and encouragement and building our scouts up.

286
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,280
I mean, that's what really works

287
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:19,840
And that's what we're supposed to be doing.

288
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:28,480
So, Heidi, you are doing exactly the right thing by encouraging uniforms at boards of review and any other scout function,

289
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:35,320
And you've got also the broad underlying concept that policies are written to encourage and support scouts.

290
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:39,000
Now, unfortunately, there are a few leaders- and I used to be one

291
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:44,000
who can misread policy and penalize and discourage scouts.

292
00:21:45,459 --> 00:21:47,939
But it does some good to keep talking about it

293
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:50,360
And I'm glad you sent me this email

294
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:55,660
And we're just going to keep talking and writing about a better approach.

